1. Algorithm reference implementation (MIT)
-------------------------------------------

  dga-diagtool
  https://github.com/ToniMellin/dga-diagtool
  Copyright (c) 2022-2026 Toni Mellin
  Licensed under the MIT License.

  Used for: transcribing the IEC 60599 (2015) ratio bands, the IEEE C57.104-2019
  Rogers and Doernenburg decision logic, and the Duval Triangle 1 zone polygons
  into dga_core/tables.py. No source file was copied verbatim; the tables and
  decision rules were re-expressed in a zero-dependency implementation.

  The upstream project also ships a ThirdPartyNotices.txt. If you redistribute
  code taken directly from dga-diagtool (rather than re-derived tables), carry
  that notice forward as well.


2. Published threshold tables (academic sources, no code copied)
---------------------------------------------------------------

  [S1] Lu, C. and Chen, ... (2014). Advanced Winding Models and Ontology-Based
       Fault Diagnosis. University of Liverpool.
       Table 1.3 "IEC code for DGA fault diagnosis".
       https://livrepository.liverpool.ac.uk/19593/4/LuChe_July2014_19593.pdf

  [S2] SSRG International Journal of Electrical and Electronics Engineering,
       Vol. 2, Issue 4, April 2015. Tables 2 and 3.
       https://www.internationaljournalssrg.org/IJEEE/2015/Volume2-Issue4/IJEEE-V2I4P101.pdf

  Used for: the classic IEC three-ratio (三比值法) 0/1/2 coding table and fault
  lookup table in dga_core/tables.py. Only factual threshold values were taken.
  See docs/STANDARDS.md for a full provenance record and the documented
  divergences between sources.


3. Datasets (NOT redistributed)
-------------------------------

  No dataset is included in this repository. Every upstream dataset repository
  carries no open-source licence, so redistributing the data would be a licence
  violation. scripts/fetch_datasets.py downloads the data on demand and verifies
  SHA-256 hashes recorded in data/manifest.json.

  - alan-456/transformer-fault-dataset (589 samples, 6 fault classes)
    https://github.com/alan-456/transformer-fault-dataset
  - Cliango/DGA (202 samples, includes a Normal class)
    https://github.com/Cliango/DGA

  Both are used here for non-commercial research and educational validation
  only. Cite the original sources, not this repository.


4. Standards referenced
-----------------------

  IEC 60599 - Mineral oil-filled electrical equipment in service: Guidance on
              the interpretation of dissolved and free gases analysis.
  IEEE C57.104 - Guide for the Interpretation of Gases Generated in Mineral
                 Oil-Immersed Transformers.
  CIGRE TB 771 - Advances in DGA interpretation.

  These are copyrighted standards documents. No standard text is reproduced
  here; only published threshold values, with their source recorded in
  docs/STANDARDS.md.
